1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,491
Hello and welcome to the Telescope.

2
00:00:01,491 --> 00:00:04,800
Every week we bring you a fresh insight from
the biggest car market in the world.

3
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,642
Now, in the previous video,

4
00:00:06,642 --> 00:00:12,440
I have explained why I stopped reviewing
XPeng products for a while in the GX review.

5
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:18,080
But this MONA L03 is going to be the restart
button of my XPeng reviews.

6
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:21,829
Because this car is so well done, so well
finished,

7
00:00:21,829 --> 00:00:26,680
that I would go as far as saying XPeng is
now a sub-brand of MONA.

8
00:00:26,680 --> 00:00:29,903
This is a very coherent and, dare I say,
original design.

9
00:00:29,903 --> 00:00:33,800
I know some people will moan that the
headlight looks like a Polestar's.

10
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,108
A Polestar is now struggling for its
existence,

11
00:00:37,108 --> 00:00:42,880
while this is going to be delivering at more
than 20,000 units per month in China.

12
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:45,364
So for most people in the world,

13
00:00:45,364 --> 00:00:49,400
this is actually the more familiar headlight
design.

14
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:53,880
Everything, every line on this car just
makes total sense.

15
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:58,920
On size, this is one size below Model Y, but
it's still on 20-inch wheels.

16
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:02,480
This is an option, and I do think it's worth
it.

17
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:04,022
Also, I need to point out,

18
00:01:04,022 --> 00:01:07,640
you only get Goodyear tyres on this 20-inch
optional package.

19
00:01:07,640 --> 00:01:12,932
The front wheel arch and the rear wheel arch
both feel very powerful,

20
00:01:12,932 --> 00:01:15,080
and a small tip at the back.

21
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,420
This is a very coherent design.

22
00:01:17,420 --> 00:01:22,960
I cannot imagine this is from the same brand
that designed the horrendous GX.

23
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:28,025
Here on the inside, this L03 is very
comfortable just being itself,

24
00:01:28,025 --> 00:01:29,840
being a 140,000 RMB car.

25
00:01:29,840 --> 00:01:35,251
By that, I mean, unlike the XPeng GX, which
is a 270,000 RMB car,

26
00:01:35,251 --> 00:01:42,160
but that car's interior is pretending to be
a 400,000 RMB car and failed miserably.

27
00:01:42,160 --> 00:01:45,373
This interior is plain and simple.

28
00:01:45,373 --> 00:01:47,833
Dare I say, in some areas, too simple,

29
00:01:47,833 --> 00:01:51,200
but you could forgive it because of the
price point.

30
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,070
And also, if you like a Tesla,

31
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:58,120
then you will like this because it doesn't
have anything it doesn't need to have.

32
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:01,360
All of the materials make sense at this
price point.

33
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:07,095
This is a very honest car — and I'm going to
repeat that word — a very coherent and

34
00:02:07,095 --> 00:02:09,720
comfortable car with its own identity.

35
00:02:09,720 --> 00:02:12,957
This car has been launched in Europe
simultaneously,

36
00:02:12,957 --> 00:02:18,060
and I can tell a bit of European influence
because I often say the huge adjustment

37
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,803
range of the steering wheel.

38
00:02:19,803 --> 00:02:23,520
Well, this is not just huge by Chinese car
standard.

39
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:26,116
This is huge by European car standard.

40
00:02:26,116 --> 00:02:30,928
A lot of people, whether you are six foot
four or very, very short female,

41
00:02:30,928 --> 00:02:35,286
anyone can easily find a very comfortable
driving position in this.

42
00:02:35,286 --> 00:02:36,640
That's the first impact.

43
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:42,840
Secondly, this car has an unusually good
rear visibility for a coupe SUV.

44
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:45,542
It's still a bit of a letterbox,

45
00:02:45,542 --> 00:02:52,636
but I will say this gives you triple the
amount of rear visibility coverage compared

46
00:02:52,636 --> 00:02:54,240
to a Tesla Model Y.

47
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:57,462
I know that's a really low benchmark to
compare against,

48
00:02:57,462 --> 00:03:02,180
but I can sense XPeng has spent some effort
trying to optimize the rear visibility

49
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:02,640
of this.

50
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:09,075
Secondly, this car's central headrest
matches with the bottom of the rear screen,

51
00:03:09,075 --> 00:03:13,206
which means this central headrest is not in
the way.

52
00:03:13,206 --> 00:03:17,140
This is unlike the Lynk & Co 07 GT I showed
you recently,

53
00:03:17,140 --> 00:03:19,280
which is completely in the way.

54
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:22,514
I can clearly see the engineering and
ergonomics

55
00:03:22,514 --> 00:03:24,805
team spend some effort to optimize

56
00:03:24,805 --> 00:03:27,800
the rear visibility of a coupe SUV like
this.

57
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:31,925
And that is very, very rare in the Chinese
car market.

58
00:03:31,925 --> 00:03:36,800
I'm now recovering from the zero-gravity
available passenger seat.

59
00:03:36,800 --> 00:03:40,840
It's in an option package, which I think
everyone should take.

60
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:44,713
I do hope the driver's seat could also have
zero-gravity seats,

61
00:03:44,713 --> 00:03:49,509
because if I want to have this kind of
experience and I'm using the car alone,

62
00:03:49,509 --> 00:03:51,415
let's say I'm charging the car,

63
00:03:51,415 --> 00:03:56,333
I do wish the front passenger seat in the
next model year update could also have

64
00:03:56,333 --> 00:03:57,440
zero-gravity mode.

65
00:03:57,440 --> 00:04:02,480
One complaint I have with the infotainment
is all of the fonts are too small.

66
00:04:02,480 --> 00:04:07,440
And this is coming from someone who uses the
smallest font on my iPhone.

67
00:04:07,440 --> 00:04:12,520
So if this is small for me, then it's too
small for just about everyone.

68
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:19,044
You can choose to enlarge the font in the
HUD and also, I believe,

69
00:04:19,044 --> 00:04:22,800
enlarge the fonts in the infotainment.

70
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:26,017
But now all of the font sizes make sense,

71
00:04:26,017 --> 00:04:32,530
but all of the icons are still too small for
the drivers and the passengers sitting

72
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:35,120
at their normal position to view.

73
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:39,441
This looks good on the design screen of that
UI designer,

74
00:04:39,441 --> 00:04:43,080
but it doesn't quite make sense here in the
car.

75
00:04:43,080 --> 00:04:44,260
Here in the rear,

76
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:50,160
the only piece of criticism I can provide is
that this car does not have a sun blind.

77
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:52,735
But given the price point, I can sort of
forgive it.

78
00:04:52,735 --> 00:04:55,120
Everything else makes total sense.

79
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:56,879
The front is set to my position.

80
00:04:56,879 --> 00:05:00,640
I can very easily tuck my feet into the
bottom of the front seat.

81
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,840
The space is fine.

82
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,080
The seat back angle makes sense.

83
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:08,040
The seat cushion is supportive while not
being too harsh.

84
00:05:08,040 --> 00:05:11,040
The central armrest is big.

85
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:15,160
I mean, I believe this car is more than 20
centimetres shorter than a Model Y.

86
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:18,560
This is clearly a class smaller than the
Model Y.

87
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:25,160
But this actually has a much better rear
cabin than a Model Y could ever dream for.

88
00:05:25,160 --> 00:05:27,347
And this is also much cheaper than a Model
Y,

89
00:05:27,347 --> 00:05:29,680
depending on where you are purchasing this
from.

90
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:36,840
In China this is a 140,000 RMB car. I'll put
its price in Europe on screen.

91
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:42,080
Yeah, this is an unusually good rear cabin
for its price.

92
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:45,800
Boot is on the smaller side.

93
00:05:45,800 --> 00:05:50,200
It's from this that you can tell this is a
Chinese car.

94
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:54,640
I would say this is barely any bigger than
the standard European hatchback.

95
00:05:54,640 --> 00:05:57,773
You do have a little bit of underfloor
storage,

96
00:05:57,773 --> 00:06:00,240
but it's nothing to write home about.

97
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:03,160
This is the pure electric version, so it
doesn't have an engine.

98
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:07,320
Therefore, you have roughly a 100-litre-ish
frunk.

99
00:06:07,320 --> 00:06:12,640
But the opening of this frunk is so deep
into the nose and it's facing the sky.

100
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:16,400
You know, taking things in and out of this
frunk is not easy at all.

101
00:06:16,400 --> 00:06:21,627
You can very easily scratch some paint when
you are offloading and loading stuff

102
00:06:21,627 --> 00:06:22,280
into this.

103
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:28,448
So much so that I don't think many people
will actually use this unless you are in a

104
00:06:28,448 --> 00:06:33,000
pinch where the boot is totally full and you
have to use this.

105
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:38,018
This is one area where I think Onvo's
Qinling will have an advantage over this if

106
00:06:38,018 --> 00:06:40,000
you don't know what that car is.

107
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:42,343
It's basically Onvo's MONA,

108
00:06:42,343 --> 00:06:49,200
Onvo's more budget-friendly line that's
supposed to come out roughly next year.

109
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:53,560
This is one area where I think the Qinling
will have the advantage.

110
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:55,760
And from this, you can tell this is a
Chinese car.

111
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:58,600
It focused more towards the rear cabin.

112
00:06:58,600 --> 00:07:04,389
But another thing I just noticed is that
this car's boot opening button,

113
00:07:04,389 --> 00:07:06,480
it's also downward facing.

114
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:10,493
If you watch my recent review of the SAIC
Volkswagen 5S,

115
00:07:10,493 --> 00:07:15,080
I said that car's boot opening button is
very difficult to find.

116
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:18,320
This is also downward facing, but it's not
difficult to find at all.

117
00:07:18,320 --> 00:07:20,720
First of all, it's completely central.

118
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:23,160
It's on the centre line of the button.

119
00:07:23,160 --> 00:07:28,440
And even if I stand very close to it, it
sticks out a little bit.

120
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,760
So I can very easily operate it blind.

121
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:35,040
I found this boot opening button on the
first try.

122
00:07:35,040 --> 00:07:40,792
I'm just saying this car, a lot of the
ergonomics, usability, ease of use,

123
00:07:40,792 --> 00:07:44,600
is clearly optimized for the European car
market.

124
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:48,320
This car has unusually good ergonomics for
an XPeng.

125
00:07:48,320 --> 00:07:53,142
Dynamically, because you can individualize
your driving mode,

126
00:07:53,142 --> 00:07:55,435
if you set steering to heavy,

127
00:07:55,435 --> 00:08:01,048
power to sport and brake pedal feel to sport
and suspension to comfort,

128
00:08:01,048 --> 00:08:06,977
that's my preferred setting, then this is a
very accomplished, dynamically,

129
00:08:06,977 --> 00:08:08,400
very polished car.

130
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:13,509
You can tell the 20-inch wheel, the optional
20-inch wheel,

131
00:08:13,509 --> 00:08:15,760
has some structural noise.

132
00:08:15,760 --> 00:08:22,026
That's kind of inevitable when you fit
wheels this big onto a car this small,

133
00:08:22,026 --> 00:08:25,200
and also it's running 45-section tyres.

134
00:08:25,200 --> 00:08:27,624
But I wouldn't say it's horrendous,

135
00:08:27,624 --> 00:08:32,957
and considering how much better looking this
20-inch wheel is compared to the

136
00:08:32,957 --> 00:08:37,320
18-inch, I'll still suggest people to choose
the 20-inch wheel.

137
00:08:37,320 --> 00:08:41,040
And also, you only get the Goodyear tyre,
which is so important.

138
00:08:41,040 --> 00:08:43,120
I mean, don't choose budget tyres.

139
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:47,864
It's the single most important component
that

140
00:08:47,864 --> 00:08:52,080
can provide the most noticeable upgrade.

141
00:08:52,080 --> 00:08:52,920
That is the tyre.

142
00:08:52,920 --> 00:08:56,320
It's the only contact patch your car has
with the road.

143
00:08:56,320 --> 00:09:00,560
And yeah, just because of that Goodyear
tyre, it's worth it.

144
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:04,449
The car we have here today is the Ultra SE
spec,

145
00:09:04,449 --> 00:09:07,528
which is the top spec of the MONA L03,

146
00:09:07,528 --> 00:09:13,280
which has the dual Turing ADAS chip that is
XPeng's in-house ADAS chip.

147
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:18,889
I do wonder how many people will choose this
spec,

148
00:09:18,889 --> 00:09:27,640
because this car has about 100 GB of memory
crammed in — for a car this cheap.

149
00:09:27,640 --> 00:09:32,593
And also, if you're watching this video two
or three years later,

150
00:09:32,593 --> 00:09:38,080
you wouldn't understand how expensive video
memory is in September 2026.

151
00:09:38,080 --> 00:09:42,515
I think most people will be better off
choosing the single Turing,

152
00:09:42,515 --> 00:09:44,800
which is the Max spec of this car.

153
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:48,200
All of these things I'm talking about only
applies to China.

154
00:09:48,200 --> 00:09:51,840
For Europe, this is a totally different
conversation.

155
00:09:51,840 --> 00:10:01,000
For the single Turing setup, XPeng has just
released the VLA 2.0 ADAS model.

156
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:03,104
That is the distilled model,

157
00:10:03,104 --> 00:10:09,040
a smaller size model compared to the dual
Turing setup that we have here today.

158
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:15,840
I do think that version is more appropriate
for this car's price point.

159
00:10:15,840 --> 00:10:20,480
I don't think many people will choose the
dual Turing setup of this car.

160
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:25,360
But still, it takes nothing away from this
car's ADAS performance.

161
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:28,452
This has the ADAS performance that other
cars

162
00:10:28,452 --> 00:10:31,200
at this price range could only dream of.

163
00:10:31,200 --> 00:10:40,085
This is top-tier performance — probably only
below FSD Beta and Huawei's ADS 5.0

164
00:10:40,085 --> 00:10:41,640
here in China.

165
00:10:41,640 --> 00:10:45,160
But this is a 140,000 RMB car.

166
00:10:45,160 --> 00:10:49,520
One other thing I have to say is this car's
design is so fantastic.

167
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:54,316
You are conscious of this car's powerful
design while you are sitting in the

168
00:10:54,316 --> 00:10:55,200
driver's seat.

169
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,514
I mean, I'll just show you.

170
00:10:56,514 --> 00:10:59,160
This is the view I'm getting looking
forward.

171
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:03,600
The front wheel arch is so powerfully in my
vision.

172
00:11:03,600 --> 00:11:07,531
And also, if I look in the mirror, both
sides,

173
00:11:07,531 --> 00:11:11,120
I can see the very powerful rear haunches.

174
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:15,680
I mean, this is a very budget friendly coupe
SUV.

175
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:19,560
And it's giving me kind of a sports car vibe
to this.

176
00:11:19,560 --> 00:11:24,640
One other criticism I have with this car is
its one-pedal driving mode.

177
00:11:24,640 --> 00:11:28,800
You can choose to turn this on in the
infotainment.

178
00:11:28,800 --> 00:11:33,657
However, that final bit of braking, just
before standstill,

179
00:11:33,657 --> 00:11:35,880
is not up there with Tesla.

180
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:37,424
I'll just quickly demonstrate.

181
00:11:37,424 --> 00:11:39,440
We are sitting at a standstill.

182
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:46,200
I'll press the brake, press the throttle.
Six, five…

183
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:49,920
I don't know if you can tell.

184
00:11:49,920 --> 00:11:59,479
There's a bit of a bouncing back, rearward
motion after coming to a standstill,

185
00:11:59,479 --> 00:12:03,351
which is not there on the Tesla.

186
00:12:03,351 --> 00:12:05,200
It's very, very subtle.

187
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:08,629
I'm not sure whether you can feel what I'm
telling you.

188
00:12:08,629 --> 00:12:11,080
Watch my head and neck movement.

189
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:18,173
The car has a tendency to move backwards
after it has come to a standstill,

190
00:12:18,173 --> 00:12:24,320
which means that final bit of braking is not
up there with Tesla.

191
00:12:24,320 --> 00:12:25,356
On the plus side,

192
00:12:25,356 --> 00:12:30,353
you can choose to have different levels of
regen with your one-pedal driving mode,

193
00:12:30,353 --> 00:12:33,400
which is a trick that so many other brands
missed.

194
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:39,113
This is one of the few Chinese brands with a
one-pedal driving mode where you can

195
00:12:39,113 --> 00:12:41,440
choose different levels of regen.

196
00:12:41,440 --> 00:12:46,560
But still, that final bit of braking, you
still need to spend some effort on it.

197
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:52,336
BYD and Geely are both looking at this
scratching their heads because they cannot

198
00:12:52,336 --> 00:12:53,120
match this.

199
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:56,160
BYD doesn't have the taste for this design.

200
00:12:56,160 --> 00:13:00,582
Having said that, I cannot believe I'm
talking about taste on an XPeng,

201
00:13:00,582 --> 00:13:05,440
having just spent a whole video criticizing
the lack of taste on the XPeng GX.

202
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,200
But this is the reality.

203
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:13,600
The much cheaper MONA L03 has much better
taste than the range-topping GX.

204
00:13:13,600 --> 00:13:19,382
Neither BYD nor Geely has anything like the
ADAS performance and also the

205
00:13:19,382 --> 00:13:21,600
infotainment design on this.

206
00:13:21,600 --> 00:13:26,120
This is, as of now, early September 2026.

207
00:13:26,120 --> 00:13:30,280
This is the best compact electric SUV in the
world.

208
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:31,720
That is all from the Telescope today.

209
00:13:31,720 --> 00:13:33,880
If you enjoyed this video, keep watching,
keep subscribing.

210
00:13:33,880 --> 00:13:36,040
More videos coming along very soon.
